# Cloudflare Workers static-assets exclusion list.
#
# The deploy's assets directory IS the repo root (/opt/buildhome/repo in the
# build container), so without this file Wrangler walks and uploads EVERYTHING
# in the checkout — including .git. That is what broke the 2026-09-06 deploy:
#
#   [ERROR] Asset too large.
#   .git/objects/pack/pack-2824a78...pack with a size of 334 MiB
#   (Workers supports assets up to 25 MiB)
#
# Same format as .gitignore. Wrangler skips anything matching a line here.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/binding/
#
# RULE OF THUMB: a path belongs here unless one of the four shipped pages
# (index.html, index2.html, IdleWorlds_Toolkit_v4_8.html, Skillsim/index.html)
# actually loads it at runtime. Everything below was checked against all four.

# ── Repo and tooling internals ───────────────────────────────────────────
# .git is not merely too big: uploading it publishes the ENTIRE history —
# every past revision of every file — as downloadable objects on the public
# site. It must never be an asset, at any size.
.git/
.claude/
.codex-tmp/
.superpowers/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.tmp

# ── Build/dev sources, never served ──────────────────────────────────────
tools/
tests/
docs/
requirements-dev.txt

# ── Source art kept in-repo for rebuilds, not loaded by any page ─────────
# ~260 MB between them. Nothing in any shipped HTML references either path
# (verified 2026-09-06); they exist so the atlases can be regenerated.
assets/zone-headers/
assets/skills-ui-atlas/

# ── Notes and internal documents ─────────────────────────────────────────
CLAUDE.md
README.txt
WOODCUTTING_CONSTRUCTION_PLAN.md
IdleWorlds-Delegated-Publisher-Trust-Addendum-v1.2A.pdf

# ── UI capture dumps consumed by tools/audit_ui_names.py ─────────────────
iw-overlay-capture.json
iw-panel-order-dungeon.json
iw-panel-order-root.json
iw-quests-capture.json

# ── DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED ────────────────────────────────────────────
# gear_icons_atlas.png / item_icons_atlas.png and their CSV/JSON manifests.
# index.html no longer fetches these at runtime (its only mention is a v4.8.4
# comment), but index2.html and IdleWorlds_Toolkit_v4_8.html still do, and both
# are deployed. Dropping them would silently blank the icons on those pages.
#
# WATCH THIS: gear_icons_atlas.png is 24.5 MB against a hard 25 MiB per-file
# ceiling. One more row of icons in the gear atlas breaks the deploy the same
# way .git just did. When it does, the fix is to retire the legacy pages or
# move the atlas to R2 — not to raise a limit that cannot be raised.
